<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- harbor:template-only
     THIS FILE IS A TEMPLATE (harbor#630). Do not cp it: @HOME@ and the other placeholders in it would be
     installed as literal text, and launchd loads such a job and then fails every time it runs. Render it:

       sh ~/port/harbor/bin/deploy-launchd-render.sh ~/port/harbor/launchd/com.harbor.usage.plist > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.harbor.usage.plist

     A cp line in the comment below predates the template. It is kept so the rendered file stays byte-identical
     to the one already installed: follow this block, not that line. This block is not installed;
     bin/deploy-launchd-render.sh drops it. -->
<!-- M9 (harbor#44) — keep the durable usage ledger alive past transcript GC.

     WHY THIS EXISTS AT ALL. Claude Code records per-message token usage in the
     session transcript, and the transcript store is garbage-collected at 30
     days. So the only durable record of what this machine spent is the one
     something writes before the transcript disappears. `status-usage-aggregate.sh`
     writes it — and until 2026-08-09 it had never been run with `--apply`, so
     there was no ledger and July was already unrecoverable by inspection.

     WHY NOT A Stop HOOK, which is what was asked for. Measured: a full run is
     10 SECONDS, and `--since` does not reduce it because the cost is walking
     every transcript, not formatting the output. Ten seconds appended to every
     session end is a delay the operator removes within a day, and CONSTITUTION
     §2.11 is explicit that a guard which blocks ordinary work is a guard that
     gets switched off. Once a day, off the session path, costs nothing anyone
     notices and loses nothing: the ledger is derived from transcripts that
     survive 30 days, so a missed day is recovered by the next run.

     TEMPLATE — launchd does not expand $HOME: replace @HOME@ with your
     home dir on install.

     AN AGENT CANNOT INSTALL THIS, BY DESIGN, and the same three floor rules that
     block the pulse job block this one: a redirect into LaunchAgents, a cp/mv/ln
     naming that path, and `launchctl load|bootstrap|setenv`. A session that can
     stand up its own scheduled job can stand up anything. Operator steps:

       sh ~/port/harbor/bin/deploy-runtime-install.sh --live --apply
       cp launchd/com.harbor.usage.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
       launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.harbor.usage.plist

     Then see it work rather than assume it — the two questions are different:

       launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.harbor.usage
       tail -3 /tmp/com.harbor.usage.out              # did the job run
       wc -l ~/.claude/MEMORY/USAGE/*/usage.jsonl     # did the ledger grow

     STDOUT IS DECLARED, NOT ONLY STDERR, for the reason the pulse job's header
     records at length: the fleet-snapshot job declares stderr alone and its
     error file has been zero bytes since installation, which is equally
     consistent with "nothing went wrong" and "the job has not run since July".
     A log that cannot separate those two states is not evidence.

     THE LEDGER IS HOST-PARTITIONED AND THIS BOX'S HOSTNAME IS NOT STABLE.
     `hostname` here has intermittently answered `Mac`, and that flip has already
     forked host-sharded ledgers in this estate. Anything READING this ledger
     must union every directory under MEMORY/USAGE/ rather than trusting one.
     Today there is a single dir; that is the current state, not a guarantee.

     DAILY, NOT HOURLY. The ledger is append-only per (day, model, entrypoint),
     so a second run in the same day rewrites the same rows rather than adding
     information. The only thing a tighter interval buys is a smaller window of
     loss if the machine dies with an un-aggregated transcript — and the
     transcript itself is that backup for 30 days. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.harbor.usage</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/sh</string>
    <string>@HOME@/.claude/bin/status-usage-aggregate.sh</string>
    <string>--apply</string>
    <string>--live</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key><integer>4</integer>
    <key>Minute</key><integer>17</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
  <key>ProcessType</key><string>Background</string>
  <key>LowPriorityIO</key><true/>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key><string>/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:@HARBOR_LOCAL_BIN@</string>
  </dict>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/tmp/com.harbor.usage.out</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/tmp/com.harbor.usage.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
